@startuml component_diagram

' =====================================================================
'  COMPONENT VIEW — the 30-second read of the architecture.
'
'  Derived from Class_Diagram/class_diag_commented.puml, which stays the
'  reference: this diagram adds nothing, it only drops everything that
'  is not a package boundary or a seam between two packages.
'
'  What it is FOR: showing that the dependency graph is a DAG, and that
'  the two engine seams (PathPlanner, MissionOrchestrator) are what keep it one.
'  Every arrow points DOWN, towards something more abstract or more
'  foundational — that is the whole design in one picture.
'
'  What it deliberately does NOT show: classes, methods, multiplicities.
'  There is currently nothing above mrta, and mrta itself has nothing
'  implementing its two seams: the scripting layer (client/), the
'  measurement layer built on it (report/), and the concrete algorithm
'  layer (algo/) were all removed, and nothing has replaced any of them
'  yet — see TODO.md.
'
'  LAYOUT: every edge carries an explicit direction and the components
'  are declared top-down in reading order. Without that, dot lays the
'  graph out by edge cost alone and the picture ends up contradicting
'  the legend that tells you to read it downward.
' =====================================================================

title Component diagram — packages, and the seams between them

skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #4A90D9
skinparam InterfaceBorderColor #C9722A
skinparam InterfaceBackgroundColor #FFF5EA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C9B458

' ── Layer 1 — the domain layer ─────────────────────────────────────
component "**mrta**\nwho does what" as mrta #FFF0F5

' ── Layer 2 — the engine seams, declared by core ──────────────────
interface "PathPlanner" as ICoord
interface "MissionOrchestrator" as IDisp

' ── Layer 3 — the foundation ──────────────────────────────────────
component "**core**\nworld · grid · tick" as core #EAF4FF

' =====================================================================
'  Relations. Solid = uses the types directly. Dashed = plugs into an
'  abstraction it does not own.
' =====================================================================

' mrta plugs into the seam core declares for it. Nothing plugs into
' PathPlanner at all right now — algo/ used to, and is gone.
mrta ..down.> IDisp : implements

mrta -down-> core : uses

' core owns the two engine seams: it declares them and calls them,
' without ever knowing who implements them.
ICoord -down- core
IDisp  -down- core

note bottom of core
  **No caller, no algorithm drawn — on purpose**
  Something still has to wire a SpatialIndex, agents and a PathPlanner
  (and a TaskDrivenOrchestrator in MRTA mode) to actually run this, and
  something still has to implement PathPlanner in the first place. Both
  used to exist — client/ wired scenarios, algo/ implemented PathPlanner
  and AssignmentStrategy — and both were removed. Nothing stands in
  their place yet — see
  TODO.md and the project's own notes on why a replacement was not
  simply reintroduced under another name.
end note

legend bottom left
  **How to read it**
  Every arrow points downward: the graph is a DAG, and **core** — at
  the bottom — depends on nothing.
    solid   A uses B's types directly
    dashed  A plugs into an abstraction it does not own
  The interfaces are where the graph would otherwise cycle: without
  them core would have to import a concrete algorithm.
end legend

@enduml
